      "summary": "The CMap comment handling and repeated-start scanning findings appear fixed. The page-text guard remains reachable only after PdfPig materializes letters, and the new preflight counts stored streams rather than repeated content references.",
      "findingList": [
        {
          "severity": "major",
          "file": "backend/AirlineDemo.Api/Evidence/IsolatedPdfParser.cs",
          "line": 148,
          "message": "The added stream-size cap does not bound repeated execution of a referenced content stream. PdfPig may materialize the expanded page letter collection before the text-length guard runs.",
          "confidence": 0.84,
          "category": "security",
          "evidence": {
            "codePathTraced": "The preflight counts each stored stream once, but PdfPig can execute the same stream repeatedly when a page's /Contents array references it multiple times. ParseCore then accesses getTextParts(page) before CanMaterializePageText enforces the extracted-text limit.",
            "failureScenario": "A PDF within the 10 MB input limit contains one 512 KiB text stream referenced repeatedly by a page's /Contents array. The preflight counts only 512 KiB, while PdfPig can materialize the repeated page letters before the guard rejects text over 8 MiB, creating a reachable resource-exhaustion path in the API process (OWASP A06:2025)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
